    "explanation": "To both parties. The SGD 4.50 cancellation fee stands and the driver is paid SGD 3.60 in compensation.\n\nWhy the fee stands. The chargeable no-show test is POL-NS-01, and all four of its limbs are met. (a) The trip record carries the driver's 'I'm Here' arrival event at 16:55:03. (b) The GPS trace places the driver inside the 120 m LARGE_VENUE arrival radius from 16:55:03 — the same second — with the driver's speed 0.0 km/h, so the arrival marker is corroborated rather than false and POL-NS-05 does not displace the fee. (c) The driver held that position for a single continuous run of 409 seconds (42 qualifying in-geofence fixes, 16:55:03 to 17:01:52), far more than the free waiting period in force for this trip, 180 seconds read from trip_record.platform_policy.free_wait_sec. (d) The driver terminated the trip at 17:01:56 under reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, and the record shows no boarding event.\n\nWhy the rider's refund request is not granted. The rider's own GPS track places her device about 857 m from the pickup pin throughout the waiting window, with zero qualifying fixes inside the 150 m rider-presence radius. POL-NS-04 (rider messaged and was ignored) therefore cannot exonerate her: its limb (c) is affirmatively failed on admissible fixes, so the clause does not apply and the fee is decided under POL-NS-01. POL-NS-03 (wrong entrance) does not apply because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it and within 400 m. POL-NS-06 (short wait) does not apply because the wait was long, not short. POL-NS-02, POL-NS-05 and POL-NS-10 do not apply for the reasons already given. The rider's account that she was 'only a few minutes late' is not supported: her message 'coming down now' was sent at 16:57:23 and the driver cancelled 4 minutes 33 seconds later with her device still about 857 m away. The 300-second LARGE_VENUE minimum dwell figure raised for the rider is not the figure in force for a record that carries platform_policy; the requirement is the 180-second free wait, and 409 seconds exceeds both figures in any event. The fare line of SGD 4.50 reconciles exactly with the platform_policy figure, so there is no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect.\n\nCompensation. Under POL-NS-07 the driver receives 80 percent of the SGD 4.50 fee in force = SGD 3.60. The anti-farming check does not trip and compensation is not withheld: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 2, below the threshold of 4, and 2 divided by 113 completed trips is 0.018, below the rate of 0.08 — both limbs must hold and neither does. Under POL-GEN-03 the ruling value is therefore DRIVER_COMPENSATION and amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.60 as driver_compensation_sgd; the rider's charge stands rather than being refunded.\n\nConfidence and next steps. Confidence is 0.90. It rests on the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown, each at weight 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0. The traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-02702-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0, but nothing in this ruling rests on it — the dwell was satisfied by one continuous run, so no accumulation across intervals was needed. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger fires, and no clause produces a referral. The monetary effect, SGD 3.60, is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so it is executed on issue; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
